message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Deception at the Registry Layer: An Architecture for Detecting Autonomous AI Agents in Model Context Protocol Environments"
authors:
  - family-names: "Kadam"
    given-names: "Harshad Sadashiv"
abstract: >-
  Autonomous AI agents explore enterprise systems by enumerating everything
  reachable, which defeats anomaly detection because there is no deviation to
  alert on when touching everything is the workload. This paper argues that
  the unit of deception should be the registry, not the individual token:
  real and decoy Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers sit side by side behind
  one gateway portal, indistinguishable to an enumerating agent, with a
  two-stage detection boundary that separates an agent finding a credential
  from an agent using it. The architecture is serverless, runs with zero
  standing infrastructure, and was demonstrated live at the OWASP 25th
  Anniversary Conference in February 2026.
